%% Kitchen order lifecycle — the KitchenTicket state machine. Every
%% transition is driven by the operator UI and stages an IntegrationEvent
%% (through the outbox). Most of those events are consumed by Ordering to
%% advance the parent Order; the bump is an audit signal only.
%%
%% Source of truth: Kitchen.API/Domain/Aggregates/KitchenTicket/KitchenTicket.cs,
%% Kitchen.API/Domain/Enums/KitchenTicketStatus.cs,
%% Kitchen.API/Domain/Enums/KitchenItemStatus.cs,
%% Kitchen.API/Endpoints/{AcceptOrder,BumpOrder,CancelOrder,MarkItemReady,MarkOrderReady,RecallOrder,StartItemPrep}.cs
%%
%% Traced by `trace_business_flow({flowName: 'kitchen-order-lifecycle'})`
%% in src/tools/flow-tracing.ts, which publishes
%% KitchenOrderAcceptedIntegrationEvent → KitchenOrderPrepStartedIntegrationEvent
%% → KitchenOrderReadyIntegrationEvent and then reads the
%% order-created-integration-event-handler queue depth.
%%
%% Last reconciled to code: 2026-10-24.

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> New : ticket created from OrderCreatedIntegrationEvent
    New --> InProgress : POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/accept (operator)
    InProgress --> Ready : POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/mark-ready (every item Ready)
    Ready --> Bumped : POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/bump (operator serves the order)
    Bumped --> Ready : POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/recall (chef pull-back)
    New --> Cancelled : POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/cancel
    InProgress --> Cancelled : POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/cancel
    Ready --> Cancelled : POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/cancel
    Bumped --> Cancelled : POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/cancel

    note right of New
        Per-item state machine (KitchenItemStatus):
        Pending → Preparing → Ready
        POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/items/{itemId:guid}/start
        POST /v1/kitchen/tickets/{id:guid}/items/{itemId:guid}/ready
        The ticket stays New/InProgress while the items move.
    end note

    note right of InProgress
        Accept publishes
        KitchenOrderAcceptedIntegrationEvent
        → Ordering marks Order.ConfirmedAt
    end note

    note right of Ready
        MarkOrderReady publishes
        KitchenOrderReadyIntegrationEvent
        → Ordering marks Order.ReadyAt
        Only legal once every item reports Ready.
    end note

    note right of Bumped
        BumpOrder publishes
        KitchenOrderBumpedIntegrationEvent
        → Ordering records it for AUDIT ONLY:
        Order.Status is unchanged and stays Ready
        until the order is dispatched.
        Recall (Bumped → Ready) raises NO integration
        event — a domain event only
        (KitchenTicketRecalledEvent) — so Ordering
        is not notified.
    end note

    note right of Cancelled
        CancelOrder publishes
        KitchenOrderCancelledIntegrationEvent
        Permitted from every non-cancelled state.
    end note
